    "checks": [
      "The code defines accessory apartment but no district permits it. Uses not listed in a district schedule are prohibited (600-608A)",
      "600-609 similar-use special exception applies only to a use not listed as prohibited. Weak path given 600-608A and the bars below",
      "R-3 lists Conversions as a conditional use, but 600-804C(4) bars converting a one-family dwelling",
      "A lot shall only be occupied by one dwelling unit unless the chapter specifically allows more (600-902C)",
      "An accessory building shall not be converted into a dwelling unit unless specifically allowed (600-902D). Human habitation in accessory buildings is prohibited (600-1001F)",
      "Conversion of an existing one-family detached, semidetached or attached dwelling into two or more units is prohibited (600-803C, 600-804C(4), 600-1203D)",
      "A detached garage may have a second story for household storage only (600-1002B). Garages and carports: 600 sq ft max in R districts unless they meet principal setbacks",
      "Closest allowed options: two-family detached dwellings and low-rise apartments are permitted by right in R-3 as new buildings. In C-C and C-R, existing building space may become dwelling units only on a lot with a street-level business (600-807, 600-808)",
      "Each dwelling unit holds one household meeting the definition of family (600-902F)"
    ],
